  ### Step 2: Understanding Endianness (Byte Ordering)

  Endianness refers to the order in which bytes of a multi-byte word are stored or transmitted.

  #### 1. Big Endian (Most Significant Byte First)

  Big Endian stores the bytes in their natural reading order (left-to-right). This matches how we write words and numbers.

  • Order: Byte 1, Byte 2, Byte 3, Byte 4, Byte 5
  • Mapping:  77  →  6d  →  68  →  74  →  64 
