  #### 2. Little Endian (Least Significant Byte First)

  Little Endian stores the bytes in reversed order (right-to-left). This is how x86 and x64 computer processors (like Intel and AMD) organize data in memory.

  • Order: Byte 5, Byte 4, Byte 3, Byte 2, Byte 1
  • Mapping:  64  →  74  →  68  →  6d  →  77 
